; A raise from an after-thunk of Chez's own dynamic-wind, which a plain
; library uses, is not taken while exit leaves the task, so a handler in
; the task can take it and the task goes on; Tuna exits once the task
; ends, not when it next pauses.
> (import (prefix (only (chezscheme) dynamic-wind) chez:))
> (begin
    (guard (c [#t (display "handler ran") (newline)])
      (chez:dynamic-wind void (lambda () (exit)) (lambda () (car '()))))
    (display "the task goes on")
    (newline)
    (sleep-for 0.05)
    (display "after a pause")
    (newline))
handler ran
the task goes on
after a pause
configuration unloading
keeper unloading
> (display "never runs")
